meta {
  name: Customer_Auth
  seq: 13
}

auth {
  mode: inherit
}

docs {
  Customer sign-in with the site key (`X-Auth-Token`, server or app). Steps:
  
  1. A new customer: `Register a customer by email` (the password is optional) → a code in the email → `Confirm the sign-in or sign-up with the code` with `confirmation_id` and the code. `confirmationId` is saved by the register request.
  2. A registered customer: `Sign a customer in` by email and password (tokens at once) or `Sign a customer in by phone` → an SMS code → `Confirm the sign-in or sign-up with the code`. The phone request saves `confirmationId`; put the code you got into the body of confirm. SMS sign-in takes only phones with the country code +7 and only on sites that allow sign-in by phone: otherwise 422 `business-rule` with `pointer` `#/phone`; such a customer signs in by email. The phone of a delivery address is not limited to +7.
  3. `customerToken` (an hour) goes to `X-Customer-Auth-Token` of `Customer_*`; when it expires — `Renew the customer token` with `customerRefreshToken` (one-time, 30 days).
  4. `Sign a customer out` with `customerRefreshToken` ends the sign-in.
  5. A guest without an account: `Get a guest token` (first in the folder) saves `guestToken` (90 days). It opens `Customer_Cart`, the address requests of `Customer_Account` and `Customer_Order` except `Cancel my order`, so a guest can order without signing in. The customer folders send `customerToken`: to run them as a guest, set the runtime variable `customerToken` to the value of `guestToken` by hand. This is the only case to set `customerToken` yourself. The profile, password and order cancel requests need a signed-in customer.
  6. A guest who signs in or up keeps the cart, orders and addresses: add `"guest_token": "{{guestToken}}"` to the body of confirm (or of sign-in by email and password). The guest token stops working after that: use the customer token.
  
  Codes are 4 digits and are really sent. A wrong code or an unknown `confirmation_id` gives 401 `unauthorized`, the same type as a missing or expired customer token: tell them apart by the request, not by the type. After 401 at confirm ask for the code again; do not renew tokens.
  
  A new code: wait `code_lifetime` seconds of the last answer (an SMS: 3 minutes after the first two codes, then 8 minutes, 30 minutes, an hour, up to 24 hours after the 10th code; an email: 55 seconds). Asked sooner, the request gives 422 `business-rule`: send the same request again after the pause. Confirm: every try counts, 5 tries in 15 minutes for one email or phone; the 6th gives 429 `sign-in-locked` with `Retry-After`, even with the right code. A code checked 5 times gives 422 `business-rule` until a new code is sent.
}
